public of China (Taiwan), Flow of Funds, JSON API files FL02_en (financial assets and liabilities) and FL01_en (financial transactions), item Shares: holders are the Assets and Use of Funds sides of the nine domestic sectors and the rest of the world, everything issued is the Liabilities side of all domestic sectors, NT$ million, yearly at 31 December","note":"Every owner is a sector of the flow of funds that Taiwan's central bank publishes once a year, at market value, in New Taiwan dollars, for 31 December; each year's figures arrive about thirteen months later. Households are what is left once the other sectors are counted, so they carry any error in the others. Non-residents are holders who live outside Taiwan. The national pension sits with the government, Chunghwa Post's savings with the banks, and mutual funds with the other financial firms. Listed shares are companies listed on Taiwan's exchanges, at market prices. For shares the central bank records as bought only the money paid for newly issued shares, so buying and selling between owners shows up in price and other changes. Source: Central Bank of the Republic of China (Taiwan), Flow of Funds, used under the Open Government Data License, version 1.0; shares of the total are our calculations."}